      "source": [
        "# Online Retail: Data Quality, Cleaning and Sales Analysis\n",
        "\n",
        "## Project objective\n",
        "Use Python to inspect transaction data, document cleaning decisions,\n",
        "visualise sales patterns, and investigate how data quality affects findings.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Questions\n",
        "- What data quality issues are present?\n",
        "- How does monthly gross merchandise sales value change?\n",
        "- Which products lead, and how sensitive are their rankings to unusual entries?\n",
        "- How is sales value distributed across countries and identified customers?\n",
        "\n",
        "## Dataset\n",
        "UCI Online Retail: transactions from a UK-based online retailer.\n",
        "\n",
        "Source: https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/352/online+retail\n",
        "\n",
        "Each row represents an invoice line, rather than a complete order.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Tools\n",
        "Python, pandas, Matplotlib, and Google Colab.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Analysis scope\n",
        "Monthly analysis covers December 2010–November 2011.\n",
        "The partial month of December 2011 is excluded.\n",
        "\n",
        "The original gross-sales view excludes cancellations, non-positive\n",
        "quantities and prices, identified non-merchandise codes, and exact repeats.\n",
        "\n",
        "A separate sensitivity view additionally excludes two investigated\n",
        "positive entries with evidence of subsequent offsets. Country and\n",
        "customer analyses use this sensitivity view.\n",
        "\n",
        "These measures are not net revenue or profit."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "2a3KsZa90Q7A"
      }
    },
